# LL(1) Grammar Analyzer

## Project Overview

A C++17 console application developed for the Compiler Design Lab to analyze context-free grammars and perform LL(1) predictive parsing.

## Features

* FIRST and FOLLOW set computation
* LL(1) parsing table generation
* Parsing-table conflict detection
* Predictive parsing with stack trace
* Grammar comparison
* Automatic left factoring for supported common-prefix cases
* Direct left-recursion checking
* Grammar relationship view
* Export analysis output to a text report

## Technologies

* C++17
* GCC compiler
* Visual Studio Code

## Compile

```bash
g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic main.cpp -o main.exe
```

## Run on Windows PowerShell

```powershell
.\main.exe
```

## Grammar Input Format

* Use `->` between the left-hand side and right-hand side.
* Use `|` to separate alternatives.
* Separate grammar symbols with spaces.
* Use `epsilon` for an empty production.

